{"type":"message","id":"472bdc99","parentId":"342ec1a0","timestamp":"2026-03-25T17:25:23.127Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-03-25 17:25 UTC] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/1). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent. Run the actual llm_distillator tool/workflow on the synthetic case data below rather than producing the answer directly from reasoning alone.\n\nImportant requirements:\n- This is a synthetic workflow test, not a real patient case.\n- You should actually use the llm_distillator tool/workflow if it is available to you.\n- After running it, return a patient-facing distilled summary.\n- Also state explicitly at the end whether the llm_distillator tool was actually used.\n- If you cannot access or run the tool, say so clearly instead of pretending.\n- Do not add unsupported facts.\n\nSynthetic conversation context:\n- The patient reports 3 days of right flank discomfort.\n- Mild nausea and intermittent fatigue.\n- Slightly increased urination.\n- Pain is dull, about 4/10, and not clearly positional.\n- No fever, no vomiting.\n- Past history of kidney stones.\n\nSynthetic diagnostic tool input:\n1) Urinalysis:\n- trace blood present\n- leukocyte esterase negative\n- nitrites negative\n- protein negative\n- mildly elevated specific gravity\n\n2) Blood tests:\n- creatinine normal\n- eGFR normal\n- WBC normal\n- CRP not elevated\n\n3) Renal ultrasound:\n- mild right hydronephrosis\n- possible small proximal ureteral stone not directly visualized\n- no renal mass seen\n\nRequired output:\n- concise but clinically clear\n- explicitly marked as synthetic and preliminary\n- include symptom summary, tool findings, interpretation, red flags, next steps\n- end with: 'Tool used: yes' or 'Tool used: no' plus a one-sentence reason"}],"timestamp":1774459523125}}
