ite blood cell elevation, or urine infection markers makes **active infection less supported** by these inputs.\n- Kidney function is reported as **normal**, which is reassuring.\n- The ultrasound does **not show a renal mass**.\n\n**Red flags**\nSeek urgent in-person medical care if any of the following occur:\n- **Fever or chills**\n- **Worsening or severe pain**\n- **Persistent vomiting**\n- **Trouble passing urine** or major drop in urine output\n- **Visible heavy blood in urine**\n- New weakness, fainting, or signs of dehydration\n\n**Next steps**\n- Arrange **clinical follow-up soon**, since mild hydronephrosis suggests at least some obstruction.\n- A clinician may consider **repeat assessment and symptom management**, and decide whether additional imaging is needed if symptoms persist or worsen.\n- Because specific gravity is mildly elevated, **hydration status may be worth reviewing**, unless a clinician has advised fluid restriction.\n\n**Tool used: no** — I attempted to run the actual `llm_distillator` workflow, but it was not usable in this environment because the Hugging Face access token returned a 401 expired-token error.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0fea83e6b3088d800169c41aa460bc8191af4eddfdd47a2a9c\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":121,"output":578,"cacheRead":10368,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11067,"cost":{"input":0.00030250000000000003,"output":0.00867,"cacheRead":0.0025919999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.011564500000000002}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774459551677}}
